<title>JAPAN: Yokogawa Elec rises on foreign buying.</title>
<headline>Yokogawa Elec rises on foreign buying.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Yokogawa Electric Corp soared on Tuesday morning, helped by active buying from foreign securities houses, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the industrial instruments maker is seen as a laggard issue among blue-chip shares.</p>
<p>At 0434 GMT, the share price of Yokogawa Electric was up 85 yen or 8.54 percent at 1,080 yen, making it the largest percentage gainer on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
<p>Its trading volume was 1.695 million shares.</p>
